#!/bin/sh
# With sleep_debug = yes in banana/bananad.conf: what each device's suspend and resume cost, from the kernel
# (pm_print_times), the slowest first, in banana/logs/sleep-devices.log. For finding what holds a wake-up up.
grep -qs '^ *sleep_debug *= *yes' /data/banana/bananad.conf || exit 0
case $1 in
pre)
    echo 1 > /sys/power/pm_print_times 2>/dev/null
    echo "banana-sleep-mark" > /dev/kmsg
    ;;
post)
    sleep 1     # the kernel's last lines in
    {
        echo "== $(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S')"
        # everything after the mark: the PM summary lines, then the 15 slowest device calls on the way back
        dmesg | sed -n '/banana-sleep-mark/,$p' | grep -E 'PM: (suspend|resume)[^,]*(took|complete|exit|entry)' | sed 's/^\[[^]]*\] //'
        dmesg | sed -n '/banana-sleep-mark/,$p' | sed -n 's/.*call \([^ ]*\)+.* returned [0-9-]* after \([0-9]*\) usecs.*/\2 \1/p' |
            sort -rn | head -n 15 | awk '{ printf "  %7.1f ms  %s\n", $1 / 1000, $2 }'
    } >> /data/banana/logs/sleep-devices.log
    ;;
esac
exit 0
